  "limitations": [
    "Early R01 independent conditional red-white twisted-frame hall scene only. Twenty-five original files and one true original commit are preserved byte-for-byte. This is loss-prevention archival, not completed reconstruction, standard delivery, source validation or user acceptance.",
    "Actual supplied sources are three 320x176 published GIFs a15/a16/a18 with112/108/96 frames and five decoded key PNGs at original resolution. They are not native livestream frames. GIF frame indices and cumulative milliseconds are not video clip timestamps; performance date, livestream/BV, calibrated cameras and highest decoded quality remain unknown.",
    "The current static hypothesis follows a16 frame27 dark-tunnel state; a15 frame110 and a16 frame107 provide conditional common-space clues. a18 bright-tunnel state is auxiliary evidence, not permission to change geometry/materials by camera. Hidden extent, back surfaces, thickness, frame count/spacing, units and props remain inferred.",
    "The frozen tree contains one editable BLEND and one GLB, not separate material/white model files. The producer describes shared MATERIAL/WHITE layers and records193 object-inference rows,11 saved camera records including8 CHECK directions and8 frame parameters. These are metadata checks, not independent Blender geometry, layer, source-camera or rendered-view validation.",
    "No model renders, direct overlays, relative-depth analysis or completed independent model/roundtrip QA are included. The existing export log explicitly warns that AREA lights are unsupported; GLB lighting appearance equivalence is not established. Eight saved CHECK cameras are not eight completed diagnostic images.",
    "Broader discovery manifests are preserved as provenance: animated-manifest.json has19 entries but only a15/a16/a18 are supplied; gif-frame-manifest.json includes an absent a05 GIF and sample-image references outside this scene freeze. The limited novelty report also cites external old-source/evidence/comment/snapshot files that are not in the25-file tree. They are not claimed delivered or independently inspected by the archive worker, and no missing research artifact is reconstructed or fetched elsewhere.",
    "The supplied limited novelty review reports a source-pixel distinction from old Issue15 and bounded29-issue text screening; this archive does not independently redo that research or claim exhaustive old-scene deduplication. The original report, research references and uncertainty are retained unchanged.",
    "A new independent archive branch is based on the unchanged verified backstage archive commit solely to preserve all11545 existing paths. The backstage branch, main and all208 preexisting advertised refs are unchanged. The original producer commit is preserved on a separate history ref; no production branch or worktree is written.",
    "Only official Library file reception, ordinary Git and fresh-remote byte/object/tree verification are performed. No modeling, rendering, producer-script execution, LFS, force push, history deletion, credential copying, security changes, Issues or PRs. The denied source-screening-increment receipt remains paused. Space and permanent attachments remain untouched; consumer-lock release is reported only after independent receipt readback."
